WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.457
We want to train on user data without exposing it.

00:00:03.537 --> 00:00:07.914
Federated learning keeps data local but exchanges
whole models,

00:00:07.994 --> 00:00:10.036
costly for large transformers.

00:00:10.116 --> 00:00:15.342
Split learning instead shares only cut-layer
activations, the smashed data.

00:00:15.422 --> 00:00:18.738
But transformers have no pooling or convolution,

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:25.246
so their smashed data barely distorts the input and
stays visually similar to the raw image.

00:00:25.326 --> 00:00:29.915
That similarity leaks privacy and, preserving so
much information,

00:00:29.995 --> 00:00:32.250
also inflates communication cost.
